WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.640
- Our next guest became
an international superstar

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:04.410
as a member of Destiny's Child,

00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:05.821
♪ I'm a survivor ♪

00:00:05.821 --> 00:00:08.682
I was, I was in the
video, in my brain movie.

00:00:08.682 --> 00:00:11.620
Since then she's gone on
to a successful solo career

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:12.600
as a singer.

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:14.540
And she's out now with a new book

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:17.251
called Checking In, say
hello to Michelle Williams.

00:00:17.251 --> 00:00:22.091
(clapping, cheering and musical intro)

00:00:22.091 --> 00:00:24.650
Hello, I am so honored
to have you on this show.

00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:25.630
I love you already.

00:00:25.630 --> 00:00:26.750
And we don't even know each other.

00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:28.040
So I sound like a stalker

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:29.710
(laughing)

00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:34.690
- Stop it, I am so excited
to be on your show.

00:00:34.690 --> 00:00:36.047
Congratulations.
- Thank you!

00:00:36.047 --> 00:00:39.300
- I just love when I see my fellow peers

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:42.460
in music transition on to other passions.

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:44.170
So thank you for having me.

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:45.770
Yeah, well, thank you so much.

00:00:45.770 --> 00:00:47.940
Speaking of transition,
you have a book out now.

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:49.140
That's amazing.

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:51.400
And I love how honest it is.

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:53.920
It's called Checking In and I feel

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:55.630
like a lot of people
are gonna relate to this

00:00:55.630 --> 00:00:57.430
and I think it might help
a lot of people get through

00:00:57.430 --> 00:00:59.360
a lot of their depression and anxiety.

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:03.010
How did you feel comfortable
enough to open up about that?

00:01:03.010 --> 00:01:06.980
- Well, I'll back back to about 2013,

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:08.180
I was doing an interview

00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:12.900
and it was so conversational
and I kind of just blurted it

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:16.760
out that I had been dealing
with depression for a long time,

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:20.520
since about seventh grade,
and fast forward to,

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:24.470
you know, 2018, I had
another incident, you know,

00:01:24.470 --> 00:01:25.890
it was a dark moment for me.

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:29.390
And I ended up having to check in,

00:01:29.390 --> 00:01:33.950
I voluntarily checked in to
a mental health facility.

00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:38.950
And I think I wanted to try to be a voice

00:01:39.470 --> 00:01:41.350
for people who, like for me, I went

00:01:41.350 --> 00:01:43.970
from the seventh grade to
my thirties without a name

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:47.260
for what I had been feeling,
which was depression,

00:01:47.260 --> 00:01:52.260
and to bring hope is
really my ultimate goal.

00:01:53.030 --> 00:01:55.780
- Well, in the book you talk
about checking in with others.

00:01:55.780 --> 00:01:57.740
So what does that mean with you?

00:01:57.740 --> 00:01:59.810
- For me, as far as
checking in with others?

00:01:59.810 --> 00:02:01.770
You know, I have a very small circle.

00:02:01.770 --> 00:02:05.660
And so during this pandemic,
we've learned to be more

00:02:05.660 --> 00:02:10.030
intentional and not take
anything for granted.

00:02:10.030 --> 00:02:13.070
You know, when we were told to lock down,

00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:14.780
I'm a home body anyways,

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:16.712
so it worked out for me.
- Me too, yeah.

00:02:16.712 --> 00:02:18.990
- I love being home.
- Me too.

00:02:18.990 --> 00:02:20.612
- I adore it.

00:02:20.612 --> 00:02:23.580
You know, but my heart goes out

00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:26.440
to people who thrive
with, you know, having to

00:02:26.440 --> 00:02:27.670
have human connection.

00:02:27.670 --> 00:02:32.670
But honey, it was a lot of,
you know, videos, FaceTiming,

00:02:33.860 --> 00:02:38.440
phone calls, texting, just
checking on each other more so

00:02:38.440 --> 00:02:39.273
than often.

00:02:39.273 --> 00:02:42.250
And I think my friendships
were actually strengthened.

00:02:42.250 --> 00:02:44.120
- That's great, I do think so too.

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:46.620
I think, especially because
a lot of us were, you know,

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:48.420
broken down jobs in a way it was kind of

00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:50.010
like we all kind of had, it was a lot

00:02:50.010 --> 00:02:51.700
of self-reflection I think a lot more

00:02:51.700 --> 00:02:54.470
than people thought was
gonna happen in 2020.

00:02:54.470 --> 00:02:56.850
But we talked with Kelly Rowland
a few months ago actually.

00:02:56.850 --> 00:02:59.010
And she said that you were in the room

00:02:59.010 --> 00:03:02.770
on Zoom for the birth of
her son, which is crazy.

00:03:02.770 --> 00:03:06.260
I mean, it's super special,
but also like what,

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:07.750
like you saw all that?

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:11.230
(laughing)

00:03:12.260 --> 00:03:14.793
- Yeah.
- Yeah. (clapping)

00:03:14.793 --> 00:03:16.623
That is friendship.

00:03:18.942 --> 00:03:23.942
- Listen, if I ever doubted my place

00:03:25.010 --> 00:03:26.563
in Kelly Rowland's life.

00:03:27.730 --> 00:03:31.593
Getting the invitation to
watch her giving birth,

00:03:32.610 --> 00:03:34.250
put all doubt out the window.

00:03:34.250 --> 00:03:35.330
- Oh my gosh.

00:03:35.330 --> 00:03:37.000
That, it would scar me.

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:38.630
Like, I'm glad I never saw that

00:03:38.630 --> 00:03:40.297
before I got pregnant, I would've never-

00:03:40.297 --> 00:03:42.017
- It was beautiful, Kelly.

00:03:42.017 --> 00:03:44.040
It was beautiful.
- I, you know, what, Michelle,

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:48.500
I'm so different, I'm
so different. (laughing)

00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:50.700
So what do you say when people ask you

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:51.880
about like a Destiny's Child reunion?

00:03:51.880 --> 00:03:53.910
I know people have to
ask about it all the time

00:03:53.910 --> 00:03:55.530
but I feel like y'all hang all the time.

00:03:55.530 --> 00:03:57.720
You're always together
probably, but you just probably

00:03:57.720 --> 00:03:59.410
aren't doing music stuff all the time.

00:03:59.410 --> 00:04:00.750
- That is correct.

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:03.790
We're not doing music at the
moment, but we're together

00:04:03.790 --> 00:04:04.840
more so than not.

00:04:04.840 --> 00:04:08.320
If it's, if it's together,
just even just yesterday

00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:10.104
doing a FaceTime chat.

00:04:10.104 --> 00:04:12.940
I love, I love the ladies.

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:15.360
I'm here for singing together again.

00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:18.080
I think we do some of the dopest music

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:21.480
and arrangements together.

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:22.860
So we'll see.

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:27.820
I'm always open to doing music
again with Beyonce and Kelly.

00:04:27.820 --> 00:04:28.653
Always.

00:04:28.653 --> 00:04:31.310
- It's just such a, yeah,
wow, the chemistry is amazing.

00:04:31.310 --> 00:04:32.143
I love you guys.

00:04:32.143 --> 00:04:33.850
I love you as well.

00:04:33.850 --> 00:04:36.730
Everybody, Michelle's book
is called Checking In -

00:04:36.730 --> 00:04:39.440
How Getting Real about
Depression Saved My Life -

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:40.590
and can save yours.

00:04:40.590 --> 00:04:41.670
You gotta check it out.

00:04:41.670 --> 00:04:43.020
We all need this right now.

